=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\" transform=\"translate(1278,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(1778,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">\u00a0</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(600,0)\"><use data-c=\"73\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-73\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>. The radius of the merry-go-round is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.452ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.373ex\" height=\"2.149ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 1933 950\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">\u00a0</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(600,0)\"><use data-c=\"6D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6D\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>. The centrifugal force on the child will be</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"50 N"},{"identifier":"B","content":"80 N"},{"identifier":"C","content":"100 N"},{"identifier":"D","content":"40 N"}],"correct_options":["D"],"explanation":"<p>To calculate the centrifugal force acting on the child, we need to find the angular velocity of the merry-go-round and then apply the formula for centrifugal force. </p>\n<p>The merry-go-round makes 1 rotation in 3.14 seconds, so its angular velocity (<mjx-container class=\"MathJa